      "side": 1,
      "message": "`into... where?`\nThe system memory originally allocated for the dma-buf, and where users will read from / write to when it\u0027s mmapped.\n`In which case, using the uncached system heap is probably pointless and slow...`\nYeah I agree, but at least it will be functionally correct. Alternatively we could refuse to map uncached buffers that end up requiring swiotlb (since I\u0027m not sure anyone would really want this outside of bringup)?\n`we still have DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC`\nThe swiotlb syncs look like they will work correctly since the cache clean/invalidation is done unconditionally there, but I think you are right for map/unmap, since the `arch_sync_dma_for_device`  would be skipped for the swiotlb address. For unmap it\u0027s possible to avoid setting `DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC`, but for the map I think we\u0027d have to call `arch_sync_dma_for_device` ourselves after finding a swiotlb buffer, or remap without `DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC`.",
